{{also|coïncide|coïncidé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|coïncider|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|coincīdēre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|coincīdō|lang=la}}, from {{term|co-|lang=la}} + {{term|incīdō|lang=la}}, from {{term|in-|lang=la}} + {{term|cadō|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-coincide.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|coincides|coinciding|coincided}}

# To occupy exactly the same [[space]].
#: ''The two squares '''coincide''' nicely.''
# To occur at the same time.
#: ''The conference will '''coincide''' with his vacation.''
# To [[correspond]], [[concur]], or [[agree]].
#: ''Our ideas '''coincide''', except in certain areas.''

